1
00:00:00,018 --> 00:00:02,018
This is why the archetype matters.

2
00:00:02,018 --> 00:00:05,036
As Jordan Peterson puts it, chaos must be confronted,

3
00:00:05,036 --> 00:00:06,345
not retreated from.

4
00:00:06,345 --> 00:00:09,909
Order, responsibility, structure, self-authorship

5
00:00:09,909 --> 00:00:12,491
is what rescues the individual from regression

6
00:00:12,491 --> 00:00:14,127
into unconsciousness.

7
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:17,545
What protects you too much will eventually imprison you,

8
00:00:17,545 --> 00:00:20,055
not because it's cruel, but because it refuses

9
00:00:20,055 --> 00:00:22,527
to release you into life.

10
00:00:22,527 --> 00:00:25,182
Most men nowadays are not broken.

11
00:00:25,182 --> 00:00:26,273
They are overprotected.

12
00:00:26,273 --> 00:00:29,691
They were loved but never released, held but never tested,

13
00:00:29,691 --> 00:00:33,982
kept safe long past the moment safety should have ended.

14
00:00:33,982 --> 00:00:35,836
They learn to stay agreeable instead

15
00:00:35,836 --> 00:00:38,818
of becoming dangerous, compliant instead of competent,

16
00:00:38,818 --> 00:00:40,891
dependent instead of sovereign.

17
00:00:40,891 --> 00:00:44,527
They mistake comfort for intimacy and attachment for love.

18
00:00:44,527 --> 00:00:47,145
They call it loyalty when it's fear, kindness,

19
00:00:47,182 --> 00:00:50,709
when it's avoidance, maturity when it's resignation.

20
00:00:50,709 --> 00:00:53,691
They live close to home, emotionally, psychologically,

21
00:00:53,691 --> 00:00:56,527
existentially, and wonder why desire fades,

22
00:00:56,527 --> 00:01:01,145
why purpose feels empty, why life never quite begins.

23
00:01:01,145 --> 00:01:04,018
A boy can live like this, a man cannot.

24
00:01:04,018 --> 00:01:07,000
And until the mother is left, not in bitterness,

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,345
but in truth, his life will never be his own.

26
00:01:11,764 --> 00:01:12,527
That's great.

27
00:01:13,436 --> 00:01:14,782
I think that's it.

28
00:01:14,782 --> 00:01:15,873
That's really what's at the heart

29
00:01:15,873 --> 00:01:18,236
of this masculinity crisis right there.

30
00:01:18,236 --> 00:01:21,255
And I know I've been saying a lot of things about women,

31
00:01:21,255 --> 00:01:24,600
but ultimately the problem with that is it's the men.

32
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,091
It's the men that are responsible for that.

33
00:01:26,091 --> 00:01:27,836
Where's the fucking father?

34
00:01:27,836 --> 00:01:29,036
I say that to my clients all the time,

35
00:01:29,036 --> 00:01:31,218
they're talking about being devoured by their mother,

36
00:01:31,218 --> 00:01:32,055
controlled by their mother.

37
00:01:32,055 --> 00:01:33,764
And I'm like, where was your dad?

38
00:01:33,764 --> 00:01:36,127
And they're like, oh, he was kind of afraid of her.

39
00:01:36,127 --> 00:01:40,382
And I was like, well, that's your problem right there, right?

40
00:01:40,382 --> 00:01:42,091
And so you've internalized that.

41
00:01:42,091 --> 00:01:45,036
Like, because if there's no man that you see standing up

42
00:01:45,036 --> 00:01:48,091
to the woman or helping create the separation,

43
00:01:48,091 --> 00:01:50,236
then you're defenseless against a devouring mother.

44
00:01:50,236 --> 00:01:51,909
And I almost think it's not even their fault.

45
00:01:51,909 --> 00:01:52,782
Like, they can't help it.

46
00:01:52,782 --> 00:01:56,018
Like, it's a natural instinct to wanna protect, right?

47
00:01:56,018 --> 00:01:59,109
And that protection can very easily become devouring.

48
00:01:59,109 --> 00:02:01,800
And if there's not a man there to create the separation,

49
00:02:01,836 --> 00:02:05,400
to hold the boundary, to redirect her energy back towards him

50
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,945
and away from the child,

51
00:02:07,945 --> 00:02:10,673
that shadow part of her is just gonna get activated.

52
00:02:10,673 --> 00:02:15,218
So, I think women have to be aware of it in themselves.

53
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:20,673
And I've talked to mothers, I've worked with mothers

54
00:02:20,673 --> 00:02:22,636
that are very aware of that part of them

55
00:02:22,636 --> 00:02:24,636
that wants to devour their children,

56
00:02:24,636 --> 00:02:28,418
wants to almost eat them, like control them forever.

57
00:02:28,418 --> 00:02:30,164
And it's hard for them to let go.

58
00:02:30,164 --> 00:02:32,055
It's really, really hard for them to let go.

59
00:02:32,055 --> 00:02:34,018
And I don't think they can do it fully

60
00:02:34,018 --> 00:02:37,945
unless there is a strong man there to facilitate that.

61
00:02:37,945 --> 00:02:42,564
And so it's men who have to pull the child

62
00:02:42,564 --> 00:02:45,218
away from the mother

63
00:02:45,218 --> 00:02:48,891
and tolerate the mother being angry with them,

64
00:02:48,891 --> 00:02:51,873
being disappointed with them, making the man bad, right?

65
00:02:51,873 --> 00:02:52,782
That's a big part of it.

66
00:02:52,782 --> 00:02:54,091
Like, you have to tolerate

67
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:55,655
your woman's anger and rage

68
00:02:55,655 --> 00:02:59,364
as you like pull her child, your child away from her,

69
00:02:59,364 --> 00:03:01,873
away from the safety and out into the world

70
00:03:01,873 --> 00:03:03,182
where it's not perfectly safe

71
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:05,145
and introduce them to danger,

72
00:03:05,145 --> 00:03:07,036
knowing that they may get hurt,

73
00:03:07,036 --> 00:03:08,782
something bad might happen out there.

74
00:03:08,782 --> 00:03:09,545
But what are you gonna do?

75
00:03:09,545 --> 00:03:10,818
This is what life is.
